<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bashkir Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1990">1990</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bashkir ASSR</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bashkir Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic was an autonomous republic of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the southern Urals, recognised in March 1919 as the first autonomous republic in the RSFSR. Its capital was Ufa from 1922. In 1990 it declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, and it became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bashkortostan">Republic of Bashkortostan</a> within the Russian Federation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bashkir-autonomous-soviet-socialist-republic.jpg" alt="Bashkir Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osipov Georgiy Nokka · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Bashkir_ASSR.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
